    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0787" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1949v05/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.01B11 Registration/11–749</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Deputy Assistant Secretary of State
                        for European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thompson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Webb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-11-07">November 7, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the conclusion of Mr. Vyshinsky’s visit, the Secretary asked what the
                    Department of Justice planned to do on the Amtorg case. I said that we
                    understood they expected to propose to the Amtorg attorneys that they enter a
                    plea of “nolle contendre”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d470-f1"/> and that the Judge
                    impose a fine. The Secretary felt we should clean up this case promptly, thought
                    that if any fine were imposed it should be a nominal one and that it should be
                    suspended. He felt that otherwise the Soviets might refuse to pay the fine and
                    the case would drag on. He suggested it would be advisable for you to discuss
                    this with the Attorney General.</p>
                <p>Mr. Battle informed me just before his departure that the Secretary had himself
                    talked to McGrath who said he would now really get into the case.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d470-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d470-f1" n="1" xml:id="d470-f1-content">
                <p>i.e., <hi rendition="#italic">nolo contendere.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d470-f2" n="2" xml:id="d470-f2-content">
                <p>This final sentence was added to the memorandum in longhand.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
